<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/businesswoman-discussing-with-disabled-woman.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 me-3 p-3" alt="Businesswoman discussing work with a woman using a wheelchair" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/representation-user-experience-interface-design-computer.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="User experience interface design displayed on a computer" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" style="text-align: justify;">
                <h2><b>Overcoming Common Challenges in Dynamics 365 Integration</b></h2>
                <p>
                    Integration delivery must account for data differences, authentication, permissions, dependencies, and operational ownership. iFOX plans these considerations early so the resulting CRM integration services are practical to test, deploy, monitor, and support.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Data Mapping and Transformation: Define how records and fields correspond, then transform formats and values where systems use different structures or business rules.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Controlled Deployment: Use test or staging activities where available, validate dependent processes, and plan deployment steps to reduce avoidable disruption to business operations.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Ownership and Support: Document process changes and responsibilities so administrators and users understand how integrated workflows operate and where issues should be investigated.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Authentication and Permissions: Review service identities, access permissions, secure API connections, and applicable organizational controls so integrations expose only the data and actions they require.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Legacy Dependencies: Account for existing systems and interfaces that must continue operating alongside Dynamics 365 until they are changed, replaced, or retired through a planned decision.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />
                <h2><b>Leveraging APIs for Smooth Dynamics 365 Integration</b></h2>
                <p>Dynamics 365 API integration can support controlled data exchange with internal and external systems when the interface, authentication model, permissions, and error behavior are understood. iFOX evaluates API and connector options against the specific integration requirements rather than assuming one pattern fits every system.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Interface Design: Define the data, operations, frequency, ownership, and failure behavior for each interface before implementation.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  APIs and Connectors: Use suitable standard APIs or connectors where they meet the requirements, and consider custom components only when the integration needs justify them.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Authentication and Access: Configure the required authentication and permissions carefully, keeping data access aligned with the systems and processes being connected.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Monitoring and Observability: Capture appropriate status, error, and processing information so teams can identify failures and review integration behavior.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Error Handling and Documentation: Define how errors are reported and retried, and document interfaces, mappings, dependencies, and support procedures for future maintenance.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
